<title>FRANCE: Poland officially becomes 28th OECD member.</title>
<headline>Poland officially becomes 28th OECD member.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland officially became the 28th member of the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development on Friday, the Paris-based group of industrial nations announced.</p>
<p>Poland, which signed up for membership in July, is the third former Soviet bloc state after the Czech Republic and Hungary to join the organisation.</p>
<p>The country hopes that the membership of the OECD will bring greater foreign investment and boost its international credit rating.</p>
</text>
